# {{SYSTEM_NAME}} consumer rebind / migration

_Examples below reference the original {{SYSTEM_NAME}} system + its consumer file; the swap / rebind /
re-audit procedure is system-agnostic._

{{SYSTEM_NAME}} source edits don't reach a consumer file until the DS context clicks **Publish Library**,
and even then consumer instances cache their old layout until they're swapped (Gotcha #20). This skill is
how the studio context **confirms a publish is actually consumed**: re-import → swap → rebind →
re-audit → verify. Run it on the consumer file `{{CONSUMER_FIGMA_KEY}}` (or whichever consumer file
is in scope). Load `skills/figma-gotchas.md` first — the steps below cite its gotchas.

> Scope: instance-level OVERRIDES only. You do NOT audit or fix the {{SYSTEM_NAME}} component's internals — those
> are the DS context's responsibility (Gotcha #27 "audit instances skip their internals"). If the fresh
> main itself is wrong, that's a DS gap, not a rebind.

---

## Pre-flight

1. **Confirm the publish landed.** `importComponentByKeyAsync(key)` returns the last *published*
   version — if the DS context hasn't published yet, you'll just re-pull the old one. Verify the
   intended change is present on the imported main (new dimensions / variant / treatment) before
   migrating anything.
2. **Inventory the targets.** List the stale instance node-IDs in the consumer file + the published
   component KEY they should point at (from `skills/ds-components.md`). Note which overrides each
   instance carries (text labels, swapped icons/images, toggles, colored glyphs) — those are what you
   must re-apply after the swap.
3. **Plan Mode for the write.** A consumer-file migration is a write; plan the per-instance list in
   `yaml` and approve before mutating.

## The procedure (per instance)

```
re-import  →  swap stale  →  rebind  →  re-audit  →  verify
 (key)        (#20)          (#21,#28)   (#27/#28)    (screenshot)
```

1. **Re-import the published main** — `const fresh = await figma.importComponentByKeyAsync(KEY);`
2. **Swap the stale instance (Gotcha #20)** — instance layout caches until republish; force the
   re-sync: `instance.swapComponent(fresh);`
3. **Rebind everything the swap reset:**
   - **Vector fills (Gotcha #21)** — `swapComponent` resets vector fills to the new main's defaults
     (e.g. `Icon/Default/Default`), dropping your colored-glyph override. Rebind each vector fill you
     had customized.
   - **Property references (Gotcha #28)** — swap/clone detach `componentPropertyReferences`: text
     nodes lose their `characters` ref (label no longer editable), swap slots lose `mainComponent`
     (icon/image swap breaks), toggled nodes lose `visible`. **Re-bind the reference FIRST, then set
     the value** — never the reverse (setting the value sets the shared default and preserves the
     binding only if the ref exists).
   - **Re-apply overrides that reset (Gotcha #20 step 3)** — labels, swapped glyphs/images, toggles
     back to the instance's intended content.
4. **Re-audit the overrides (Gotchas #27 / #28)** — at the instance/override level only: confirm each
   text node has its `characters` ref (editable), each swap slot its `mainComponent` ref, each toggled
   node its `visible` ref; and that any NEW frame you built *outside* an instance has zero unbound
   visible properties. Target zero `NONE`. (Do not walk {{SYSTEM_NAME}} instance internals.)
5. **Render-verify** — `figma_get_component_image` (REST) to confirm the change shows and overrides
   survived. `figma_capture_screenshot` can hang the Desktop Bridge right after writes — prefer the
   REST image, or wait a few seconds.

## Per-file report (what to return)

For each consumer file / page swept, report a row:

| File / page | Instances swapped | Overrides re-applied | Audit (unbound) | Verified | Notes / gaps |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|

- **Audit** must read `0 unbound` to count as migrated.
- **Notes / gaps** — anything that couldn't be re-applied, or a defect in the fresh main → route to
  the DS context as a {{SYSTEM_NAME}} gap (don't hand-fix the component here).

## When to use which surface

- **This skill, interactively** — one file at a time, when you want to watch each swap + verify.
- **`consumer-migrator` agent** — hands-off sweep across multiple consumer files/pages, returns the
  per-file table above. Worth it because a single {{SYSTEM_NAME}} publish usually fans out over many screens.

## Common traps (from the gotchas)

- Re-importing before the DS context publishes → you migrate onto the *old* main. Always pre-flight.
- Setting `.characters` / `swapComponent` before re-binding the ref → mutates the SHARED default and
  can leak across variants (Gotcha #28 #2). Re-bind first.
- Treating a wrong fresh main as a rebind problem → it's a DS gap. Stop and route it.
